popper NEWS -- history of user-visible changes.

This is the news of e8-popper, the E8 port of popper.  'C-h P' shows
it under the package's description.


* Changes in popper 0.1.0

This is the first release, a port of popper 0.4.8.  It needs E8 0.3.1
or newer.

** 'popper-mode' makes the buffers you name popups one key toggles.
Popper binds no keys: bind 'popper-toggle' and 'popper-cycle'
yourself.

** 'popper-reference-buffers' says which buffers are popups.
An entry is a regexp the name matches, a major mode, or a function of
the name.  An entry [entry, "hide"] keeps those popups hidden when
they open, until 'popper-toggle' shows them.

** 'popper-toggle' hides the popup shown last, or shows the last hidden.
With 'C-u' it shows the next popup beside the open one; with 'C-u C-u'
it hides them all, or shows all of the group when none is open.

** 'popper-cycle' and 'popper-cycle-backwards' show the next popup.
They hide the open popup first.

** 'popper-toggle-type' makes a buffer a popup, or a popup a buffer.

** 'popper-kill-latest-popup' kills the popup shown last and its window.

** 'popper-group-function' groups popups by project or by directory.
Set it to 'popper-group-by-project' or 'popper-group-by-directory';
toggling and cycling then see only the current group's popups.

** A popup's mode line starts with " POP".
'popper-mode-line' and 'popper-mode-line-position' change it.

** 'popper-display-control' says whether popper shows popups itself.

** 'popper-open-popup-hook' runs in a popup's buffer when it is shown.
